QEMU 11.0.0, as tv-emu's setup.sh builds it on Linux (--experimental-qemu).

ui/dbus: a guest that sets a scanout without a texture no longer ends QEMU on a
failed assertion (dbus_scanout_texture: Assertion 'tex_id' failed) while a
listener for GPU buffers is there. The listener is told that the display is off.

--- a/ui/dbus-listener.c	2026-11-25 21:01:28.564621897 +0100
+++ b/ui/dbus-listener.c	2026-11-25 21:01:28.577621685 +0100
@@ -597,7 +597,15 @@
     uint32_t offset[DMABUF_MAX_PLANES], stride[DMABUF_MAX_PLANES], fourcc;
     uint64_t modifier;
 
-    assert(tex_id);
+    if (!tex_id) {
+        /*
+         * A resource without a texture, which a guest sets as it takes its
+         * display back from the GPU (at shutdown): there is no picture to
+         * hand out.
+         */
+        dbus_scanout_disable(dcl);
+        return;
+    }
     if (!egl_dmabuf_export_texture(tex_id, fd, (EGLint *)offset, (EGLint *)stride,
                                    (EGLint *)&fourcc, &num_planes, &modifier)) {
         error_report("%s: failed to export dmabuf for texture", __func__);
